          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observed a cone-shaped object with extraordinary brightness moving slowly in a zigzag pattern before disappearing over the horizon behind trees. The observation of a white glowing shape crossing the sky in a matter of minutes, on a weekend night, strongly suggests a Thai lantern, likely released nearby after a private party. The very slight movement was observed to the northwest, which is consistent with the near-zero (or very light south) wind reported at Orly: weather. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B,\" a probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
